=====================

 S~S Repository and Version Control Vocabulary

------------------------------------------

    SimpleSal source code content is published through a version control system known as GitHub.
    GitHub allows a developer to create a "repository" of content accessible throughout the world.

    The "repo" content and information about the repo's content is presented to humans and computers.
    Information about the repo's content, in human or computer form, is called "the metadata".

    The specification of the style and content of human metadata is made by the content publisher.
    The software development culture around the developer is also made by the content publisher.

------------------------------------------

=====================

 S~S Metadata about the managed object contents

------------------------------------------

    Text files with Ascii characters are used to publish metadata in several categories.

    The directory structure convention some GitHub users follow is the managed object is the set
    of source files in the same directory as the metadata files.  This intermixes types of files;
    repository Apps have, as a result, sophisticated filter and mask tools to keep it straight.

    The convention TSC LLC follows is that the metadata files exist in the repo root as above,
    while the managed object collection of files exist in a directory in the repo root itself.

    This repo contains the templates suggested or followed by TSC LLC for version control.

        1) version control (RELEASE, CHANGELOG, FUTURES);
        2) licensing (LICENSE, COPYING, COPYING-TSC-LLC);
        3) a window into understanding what the managed object is or does (README).

        .\RELEASE                   instantaneous description of a release of content at Time X
        .\CHANGELOG                 cumulative RELEASE descrptions at Time X, Y, Z
        .\FUTURES                   a hallucination, a dream, customer demand about the content

        .\LICENSE                   as emitted by GitHub license Application: GPL 3.0 selected
        .\LICENSE-TSC-LLC           an interpretation of what TSC LLC wants the license to be
        .\COPYING                   a clear statement that copying and using needs no license

        .\README                    an introduction, a window, a sales pitch about the content

        .\master-format-example     TSC LLC view of a format

